# Prettier and CI (Linux) use LF; this stops Windows autocrlf checkouts from failing `format:check`.
* text=auto eol=lf
# The tapped sidecars are checked byte for byte (the scorecard baseline stores each .beats.json's SHA-256), so git never
# converts them.
.debug-in/** -text
# Radiance HDR files start with a text header, so text=auto could treat one as text and convert its line endings.
*.hdr binary
